Interpret the following as mathematical-integer pseudocode with constant-cost arithmetic and print operations. Which offered Big-O upper bounds on the full running time are valid? Select all that apply; the bounds need not be tight.
for i=0,...,n−1:
  for j=i,...,i²−1:
    if j mod i == 0:
      for k=0,...,j−1: print("*")
An upper limit below the lower limit makes an empty loop.

For integer n>=0, determine the tightest listed growth bound for this mathematical-integer pseudocode. Arithmetic, loop-control operations and each print operation have unit cost; ignore output-digit length.
function someFunction(n) {
    for (i=0; i<10*n; i=i+1) {
        print(n);
    }
}
